0. This repository is public. That is not a licence.
----------------------------------------------------

The source is visible so that a prospective or existing customer can read it,
audit it, and see exactly what a server they run inside their network does.
Visibility is deliberate and it grants nothing: absent a Commercial Agreement
under section 2, you may read this repository and you may not use it.

Said plainly here because the opposite is the common assumption. A public
repository with no licence file is "all rights reserved" by silence, which
leaves everyone guessing; this file replaces the guess with a statement.

1. Ownership
